<description>
**Problem:** Full chainstate compaction can temporarily require nearly another copy of the database before old files are deleted.

**Fix:** Log automatic full compaction start and finish at info level. Before starting, check the free space on the chainstate filesystem, and if it is below `m_assumed_chain_state_size`, log a warning and skip this compaction. Skipping avoids the temporary extra disk use but leaves obsolete data taking up space.

Fixes #36585
</description>

<commits>
19b1126d5d logging: show automatic chainstate compaction

Automatic chainstate compaction can use substantial disk space and take minutes, but its start and finish are hidden unless `-debug=coindb` is enabled.
Log both by default so operators can identify the cause of sudden changes in disk usage.

a3de791941 coins: skip compaction if disk space is low

Full chainstate compaction can temporarily write nearly another copy of the database before deleting its input tables.

Before starting automatic full compaction, check the free space on the chainstate filesystem. If it is below the chain's `AssumedChainStateSize()`, log a warning and skip this compaction. Skipping avoids the temporary extra disk use but leaves obsolete data taking up space.

f404c06a2c doc: add chainstate compaction release note
</commits>

